    <statement><p><p>The table shows the masses, in kg (to the nearest kg), of <m>{57}</m> sheep at Kajiado market.</p><p>(a) Complete the cumulative frequency column.</p><tabular border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Mass (kg)</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Frequency (<m>f</m>)</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Cumulative frequency (cf)</cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{15}</m>–<m>{19}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{2}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><fillin characters="3" name="c1"/> </cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{20}</m>–<m>{24}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{4}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><fillin characters="3" name="c2"/> </cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{25}</m>–<m>{29}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{12}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><fillin characters="3" name="c3"/> </cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{30}</m>–<m>{34}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{15}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><fillin characters="3" name="c4"/> </cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{35}</m>–<m>{39}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{12}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><fillin characters="3" name="c5"/> </cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{40}</m>–<m>{44}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{12}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><fillin characters="3" name="c6"/> </cell></row></tabular><div/><p>(b) A cumulative frequency curve is drawn for these data.</p><div>The curve starts at the point <m>\big(</m> <fillin characters="5" name="ans7"/> <m>,\ 0\big)</m>.  </div><p>(c) At what value of <m>x</m> is the cumulative frequency for the class <m>{25}</m>–<m>{29}</m> plotted?</p><div><m>x =</m> <fillin characters="5" name="ans8"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>The cumulative frequency at an upper class boundary counts every value below that boundary. Each cumulative frequency is a running total: add each frequency to the one above it. The last one is the total, <m>{57}</m>.</p><tabular border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Class</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>f</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">cf</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Upper class boundary</cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{15}</m>–<m>{19}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{2}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{2}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{19.5}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{20}</m>–<m>{24}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{4}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{6}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{24.5}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{25}</m>–<m>{29}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{12}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{18}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{29.5}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{30}</m>–<m>{34}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{15}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{33}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{34.5}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{35}</m>–<m>{39}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{12}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{45}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{39.5}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{40}</m>–<m>{44}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{12}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{57}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{44.5}</m></cell></row></tabular><p>(b) The data are to the nearest whole number, so the first class really starts at the lower class boundary, <m>{14.5}</m>. No values lie below it, so the curve starts at <m>({14.5},\ 0)</m>.</p><p>(c) Every value in <m>{25}</m>–<m>{29}</m> is below the upper class boundary, <m>{29.5}</m>, so the cumulative frequency <m>{18}</m> is plotted at <m>x = {29.5}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>2</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>6</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>18</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>33</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>45</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>57</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{29}{2}</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{59}{2}</m></p></answer>
